From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:06:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] agent: preserve WSC recovery past configuration renew

A strict persistent reconstruction proved that the recovery ownership added
for device initialization also applies to configuration renewal.  An Agent
with retained identity enters the same per-radio WSC exchange under a
cfg_renew command.  If the shared renewal command reaches its generic TTL
while a radio is still in wsc_m2_pending or owconfig_pending, resetting that
radio to unconfigured discards the bounded recovery transaction just as the
device-init path did.

Treat both onboarding commands alike.  Their shared orchestration lifetime is
allowed to end, but an incomplete per-radio WSC transaction keeps its state
until its own bounded retry completes.  All other command and state timeout
behavior remains unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp b/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
index 2222222..3333333 100644
--- a/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
@@ -64,20 +64,22 @@ void em_orch_agent_t::orch_transient(em_cmd_t *pcmd, em_t *em)
     if (stats->time > EM_MAX_CMD_GEN_TTL) {
         em_printfout("Canceling cmd: %s because time limit exceeded\n", pcmd->get_cmd_name());
         em_state_t state = em->get_state();
         em_cmd_type_t cmd_type = pcmd->get_type();
         cancel_command(cmd_type);
-        if (cmd_type == em_cmd_type_dev_init &&
-                (state == em_state_agent_wsc_m2_pending ||
+        if ((cmd_type == em_cmd_type_dev_init ||
+             cmd_type == em_cmd_type_cfg_renew) &&
+                (state == em_state_agent_wsc_m2_pending ||
                  state == em_state_agent_owconfig_pending)) {
             // WSC is a per-radio protocol transaction and its bounded retry
-            // remains live after the shared device-init command is gone.
+            // remains live after the shared onboarding command is gone.
+            // The per-radio state is the ownership boundary, not the command.
             // Do not erase that ownership state on the generic command TTL.
-            em_printfout("Preserving %s after device-init timeout for radio %s",
+            em_printfout("Preserving %s after onboarding command timeout for radio %s",
                 em_t::state_2_str(state),
                 util::mac_to_string(em->get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str());
         } else if (state < em_state_agent_topo_synchronized) {
 	    	em->set_state(em_state_agent_unconfigured);
 		} else {
 	    	em->set_state(em_state_agent_topo_synchronized);
 		}
 	}
